As for agenda-laden?

My current agenda runs something like this.  I've found myself writing
a roguelike.  Doing so exposes one to many of these questions from the
game design side.  I thus don't like the idea that the DevTeam should
be shackled and forced to treat all playstyles as sacred.  It could be
that they like pudding farming.  Nethack 4.0 may greatly expand on
pudding farming, providing the ability to breed puddings and raise your
own pet super-pudding.  If they decide this, then the nuances of
pudding farming shouldn't be driven by the whines of Ascension-driven
players.

We've already seen a post-Nethack game which goes for a tighter midgame
clock.  Crawl, I understand, has a strong clock throughout it's game.
Thus, some people prefer it to Nethack, and some prefer Nethack to it.


I wouldn't call the authors of Crawl unethical because they didn't
